"a2s-62" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;curved=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontFamily=Verdana;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" value=""><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="a2s-71" edge="1" parent="a2s-ops" source="a2s-62" target="a2s-64" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;curved=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontFamily=Verdana;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" value=""><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="a2s-info" parent="a2s-0" value="a2s-info" /><mxCell id="a2s-infobox" parent="a2s-info" style="text;html=1;spacing=20;spacingTop=-30;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=1;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Helvetica;fillColor=#7EA6E0;strokeColor=none;arcSize=4;glass=0;shadow=0;opacity=25;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;line-height: 120%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;audio2score Flow&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify; line-height: 120%;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;How a short audio clip becomes separated stems, MIDI and engraved scores. The app is anonymous: anyone can use it, limited by API throttling and a daily quota per IP. It lives in five stacks: &lt;b&gt;Storage&lt;/b&gt; (shared bucket, table, topics and budget), &lt;b&gt;Image&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Worker&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;API&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;Web&lt;/b&gt;. Nothing is kept: files are deleted after one day and jobs after 24 hours.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;b&gt;User&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➊&lt;/font&gt; opens the single-page app through &lt;b&gt;CloudFront&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➋&lt;/font&gt;, which serves it from the private &lt;b&gt;Web Bucket&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➌&lt;/font&gt;. The app talks to the &lt;b&gt;HTTP API&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➍&lt;/font&gt;: the &lt;b&gt;ListInstruments Lambda&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➎&lt;/font&gt; returns the instrument catalog, modes and limits that the form uses.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To start a job, the &lt;b&gt;CreateJob Lambda&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➏&lt;/font&gt; validates the request (mode, instruments, size and duration), counts it against the daily quota of the caller (the IP is stored hashed) and saves the job in the &lt;b&gt;Jobs Table&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➐&lt;/font&gt;. It answers with a signed upload form that only accepts one file under the size limit, so the browser uploads the audio straight to the &lt;b&gt;Files Bucket&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➑&lt;/font&gt; without going through the API.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The new upload triggers the &lt;b&gt;Dispatch Lambda&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➒&lt;/font&gt;, which writes the worker request next to the audio, marks the job as queued and invokes the &lt;b&gt;SageMaker Async Endpoint&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;➓&lt;/font&gt;. The endpoint runs the image from the &lt;b&gt;Worker Image Repository&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;⓫&lt;/font&gt; on a GPU instance, one job at a time: it separates the stems (Demucs), transcribes them (Basic Pitch and a drum detector), quantizes rhythm, estimates the key and engraves the score with music21 and MuseScore. While it runs it writes the current stage to the job, and at the end it uploads every result to the bucket.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;SageMaker then publishes to the &lt;b&gt;Inference Success / Error Topics&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;⓬&lt;/font&gt;. The &lt;b&gt;OnComplete Lambda&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;⓭&lt;/font&gt; reads the worker summary from the bucket and marks the job as done, or as failed keeping the worker's error message.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Meanwhile the app polls the &lt;b&gt;GetJob Lambda&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(103, 171, 159);&quot;&gt;⓮&lt;/font&gt;, which returns the status, the progress of each stage and, when the job is done, short-lived signed links to download the stems, MIDI, MusicXML and PDF directly from the bucket.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The GPU is the only real cost, so the endpoint scales to zero. Its queue metrics &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➊&lt;/font&gt; feed &lt;b&gt;CloudWatch Alarms&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➋&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;b&gt;Application Auto Scaling&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➌&lt;/font&gt;: an alarm starts an instance when jobs wait with no capacity, and the instance is removed about ten minutes after the queue empties (the first job after idle waits several minutes). Other alarms catch an endpoint that does not scale back to zero, a stuck queue or repeated failures; together with the monthly &lt;b&gt;AWS Budget&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➍&lt;/font&gt; they notify the &lt;b&gt;Notifications Topic&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➎&lt;/font&gt;, which emails the &lt;b&gt;Owner&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(0, 127, 255);&quot;&gt;➏&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="2060" y="40" width="720" height="600" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>
